#!/usr/bin/python3 -IS
"""fuzz-filer: file one private security advisory on nifeos/nife for each held fuzz finding.

    fuzz-filer run [--dry-run] [--max N] [--fuzz-home DIR] [--ledger PATH] [--token-file PATH]
                   [--token-group GROUP] [--api URL] [--pace SECONDS]
    fuzz-filer ledger [--ledger PATH]

`run` reads the held directory of nife's continuous fuzz supervisor (`<fuzz-home>/state/held/`) and
its `state/windows.tsv`, and files a draft repository security advisory on nifeos/nife for each held
log that has none yet. It is a plain program, not an agent and not a language model.

- A finding is one held log, named by its content: the first 16 hexadecimal digits of the SHA-256
  of the log's bytes. The same log under two names is one finding.
- Many held logs share one cause: every log differs in its seed, its timings and its build lines,
  but a driver that trips the same check at the same place prints the same panic. Each log has a
  signature, the driver, the class, the panic's source file without its line number, and the
  panic's message with the `(replay: ...)` suffix removed and every hexadecimal number, decimal
  number and bracketed list replaced by a placeholder; its short form is the first 12 hexadecimal
  digits of the SHA-256 of those four fields. One advisory is filed per signature, for the oldest
  held log of it. Later logs with the same signature are not filed; the ledger keeps a count of them
  and the newest commit. A log with no panic line falls back to its first line that names a panic
  or carries a replay command, and a hang, which has neither, is one signature per driver.
- The ledger (`/var/lib/fuzz-filer/ledger.tsv`, owned by the account the filer runs as, mode 0600)
  records each finding as `pending` before the create call and `filed` with the advisory id after
  it, with the signature's short form as a fifth field, and one `cause` line per signature (its
  advisory, how many later logs share it, the newest commit). A finding whose last line is `filed`
  is never filed again, and neither is a signature the ledger or an advisory already covers. A
  ledger from before signatures, whose lines have four fields, still reads: its filed findings
  cover their own logs' signatures.
- Before it creates anything, it lists the repository's advisories once and reads the `Finding:`
  line of each. A finding already on GitHub is recorded as filed and not created again, and its
  signature is covered, which covers
  a run that died between the create and the ledger line, and a lost ledger. A failed listing files
  nothing.
- Each advisory names the package `nife` in the ecosystem `other` and a `vulnerable_version_range`
  of `<= <commit>`, the commit the window ran at. It sets no `patched_versions`, because no fix is
  known when a finding is filed. GitHub refuses to publish an advisory without a package and range.
- The advisory's description holds the class, the driver, the commit, the seed (or, for a crash or
  a hang, the window's first seed and count) and the one-line replay command. Its summary holds the
  finding id and the class and no seed. It never holds the signature or the panic.

It reads the `filer` token that `fuzz-token` writes (`/run/fuzz-token/filer.env`) and never the App
key. It refuses, before it opens the held directory, a token file that is a link, is not owned by
root, has a mode other than 0440, has a group other than `fuzz-token-filer`, records permissions
other than `repository_advisories:write` or repositories other than `nifeos/nife`, or expires in
less than 10 minutes.

It never writes a seed, an input, a held log's name, a panic message or file, a signature's fields
or an advisory body to standard output, standard error, the journal or the ledger. Its lines name
finding ids, signature short forms, ages, advisory ids, counts and HTTP statuses. Every message, GitHub's included, passes through a filter that replaces each seed,
held log name and token it has seen.

Rate: it files at most `--max` advisories a run (default 10), one a second, and stops the run when
GitHub reports fewer than 100 requests left this hour, or answers 403 or 429 for a rate limit; it
then exits 75 and the next run continues. It follows only `next` links back to the same listing.

`--dry-run` checks the token, reads the findings and prints what it would file, by id and age, and
sends nothing. `ledger` prints the ledger's ids, states, advisory ids and ages, and each cause's advisory, count
and newest commit.

Exit status: 0 when every finding is filed, 1 when anything was refused (each refusal is a journal
line naming the finding id and age), 75 when a rate limit stopped the run, 3 on a refusal of the
whole run (the token, the ledger, the held directory or windows.tsv) before anything is sent, 4 on an
internal error.

`--fuzz-home`, `--ledger`, `--token-file`, `--token-group`, `--api` and `--pace` exist for the
selftest and for a drop-in; the installed unit passes none of them. `--api` accepts
https://api.github.com and plain http to a literal loopback address and nothing else, and every
HTTP redirect is refused.

Name: provisional, as are the subcommands, the paths, the finding id's form, the package name, the
range's form and the summary's wording. docs/fuzz-filer.md has the install steps.

BUGS

- The count of a crash or hang window is the supervisor's `ask` (1000000), copied here because the
  supervisor records it nowhere. If the supervisor changes it, this copy is wrong until updated.
- The replay command is written from the supervisor's own build steps and has not been run by a fix
  lane yet.
- Whether GitHub accepts a commit in a `vulnerable_version_range` for the ecosystem `other` is
  unverified; a refusal is a 422, which this program reports and retries on its next run.
- Python cannot wipe memory, so the token stays in this process's heap until it exits.
"""

import argparse
import errno
import fcntl
import grp
import hashlib
import ipaddress
import json
import os
import re
import stat
import sys
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
from datetime import datetime, timezone

OWNER = "nifeos"
REPOSITORY = "nife"
FULL_NAME = OWNER + "/" + REPOSITORY
ADVISORIES_PATH = "/repos/%s/%s/security-advisories" % (OWNER, REPOSITORY)

DEFAULT_API = "https://api.github.com"
DEFAULT_TOKEN_FILE = "/run/fuzz-token/filer.env"
DEFAULT_TOKEN_GROUP = "fuzz-token-filer"
DEFAULT_LEDGER = "/var/lib/fuzz-filer/ledger.tsv"

# What the filer token must record, as fuzz-token writes it.
WANT_PERMISSIONS = "repository_advisories:write"
TOKEN_MODE = 0o440
# The token file's owner. The selftest, which cannot make root's files, changes it in process.
TOKEN_OWNER_UID = 0
# Same permissive allowlist as fuzz-token (installation tokens are now ghs_APPID_JWT, about 520
# characters with dots and hyphens); see TOKEN_SHAPE there.
TOKEN_SHAPE = re.compile(r"(?!-)[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,1024}")
# A token with less than this left is stale: the mint timer runs every 20 minutes and leaves 40.
MIN_TOKEN_SECONDS = 10 * 60
# fuzz-token mints one-hour tokens; a file claiming more was not written by it.
MAX_TOKEN_SECONDS = 61 * 60

LEDGER_MODE = 0o600
LEDGER_DIR_MODE = 0o700

DEFAULT_MAX = 10
DEFAULT_PACE = 1.0
RATE_FLOOR = 100
MAX_PAGES = 50
EX_TEMPFAIL = 75

# The supervisor's names and forms (nifeos/nife, helpers/continuous-fuzz.sh).
HELD_NAME = re.compile(r"^[0-9]{8}T[0-9]{6}Z-([0-9]{1,20})\.log$")
REPLAY = re.compile(rb"replay: (NIFE_[A-Z_]+_SEEDS)=([0-9]{1,20}):1")
SLOT_LINE = re.compile(rb"continuous-fuzz: slot [0-9]+: ([a-z-]+), seeds from ([0-9]{1,20}),")
HELD_CLASSES = ("held-finding", "held-crash", "held-hang")
DRIVERS = {
    "kernel-thread": {"variable": "NIFE_SYSCALL_FUZZ_SEEDS", "filter": "seeded_syscalls"},
    "confined": {"variable": "NIFE_CONFINED_FUZZ_SEEDS", "filter": "a_confined_fuzzer"},
}
# The supervisor's `ask`: the seed count a window is built with.
WINDOW_SEEDS = 1000000

PACKAGE = {"ecosystem": "other", "name": "nife"}
FINDING_ID = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{16}$")
SIGNATURE_ID = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{12}$")
FINDING_LINE = re.compile(r"^- Finding: ([0-9a-f]{16})$", re.MULTILINE)
GHSA_ID = re.compile(r"^GHSA(-[23456789cfghjmpqrvwx]{4}){3}$")

# A panic line, in the current form (`panicked at FILE:L:C:` then the message on the next line) or
# the older one (`panicked at 'MESSAGE', FILE:L:C`).
PANIC_AT = re.compile(r"panicked at (?:'(.*)', )?([^\s:']+):[0-9]+(?::[0-9]+)?:?\s*(.*)$")
REPLAY_SUFFIX = re.compile(r"\s*\(replay:[^)]*\)")
BRACKETED = re.compile(r"\[[^\]]*\]")
HEX_NUMBER = re.compile(r"\b0[xX][0-9a-fA-F]+\b")
DECIMAL_NUMBER = re.compile(r"(?<![A-Za-z_<])[0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)?")
MAX_LINE = 4096

# Every string that must never be printed: the token, each seed, each held log's name.
SECRETS = []


class Refusal(Exception):
    """A failure with a message meant for a person, printed without a traceback."""


class RateLimited(Exception):
    """GitHub asked this run to stop."""


def redact(text):
    text = str(text)
    for s in sorted(set(SECRETS), key=len, reverse=True):
        if s:
            text = text.replace(s, "[withheld]")
    return text


def say(text, err=False):
    print("fuzz-filer: " + redact(text), file=sys.stderr if err else sys.stdout, flush=True)


def secret(value):
    value = str(value)
    if value:
        SECRETS.append(value)
    return value


def age_text(seconds):
    seconds = max(0, int(seconds))
    if seconds < 3600:
        return "%dm" % (seconds // 60)
    if seconds < 172800:
        return "%dh" % (seconds // 3600)
    return "%dd" % (seconds // 86400)


def utc_now():
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc)


def utc_text(when):
    return when.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def parse_utc(text):
    try:
        return datetime.strptime(text, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ").replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        raise Refusal("the timestamp %r is not a UTC timestamp" % (text,))


# The token.

def read_token(path, group_name):
    """The token, after every check on its file and its recorded fields. Refuses otherwise."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC | os.O_NOCTTY |
                     os.O_NONBLOCK)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Refusal("the token file %s cannot be opened: %s (a link is refused); is "
                      "fuzz-token@filer.timer running?" % (path, e.strerror))
    try:
        st = os.fstat(fd)
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
            raise Refusal("the token file %s is not a regular file" % path)
        text = os.read(fd, 65536).decode(errors="replace")
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    fields = {}
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if line and not line.startswith("#"):
            k, _, v = line.partition("=")
            fields[k] = v
    token = fields.get("GH_TOKEN", "")
    if token:
        secret(token)
    problems = []
    if st.st_uid != TOKEN_OWNER_UID:
        problems.append("it is not owned by uid %d (root)" % TOKEN_OWNER_UID)
    if stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode) != TOKEN_MODE:
        problems.append("its mode is %04o, not %04o" % (stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode), TOKEN_MODE))
    try:
        group = grp.getgrgid(st.st_gid).gr_name
    except KeyError:
        group = "gid %d" % st.st_gid
    if group != group_name:
        problems.append("its group is %s, not %s" % (group, group_name))
    if not TOKEN_SHAPE.fullmatch(token):
        problems.append("it holds no token of the expected shape")
    if fields.get("GH_TOKEN_PERMISSIONS") != WANT_PERMISSIONS:
        problems.append("it records the permissions %r, not %s (the wrong profile?)"
                        % (fields.get("GH_TOKEN_PERMISSIONS"), WANT_PERMISSIONS))
    if fields.get("GH_TOKEN_REPOSITORIES") != FULL_NAME:
        problems.append("it records the repositories %r, not %s"
                        % (fields.get("GH_TOKEN_REPOSITORIES"), FULL_NAME))
    try:
        left = (parse_utc(fields.get("GH_TOKEN_EXPIRES_AT")) - utc_now()).total_seconds()
        if left < MIN_TOKEN_SECONDS:
            problems.append("it expires in %d seconds, less than %d (stale; is "
                            "fuzz-token@filer.timer running?)" % (left, MIN_TOKEN_SECONDS))
        elif left > MAX_TOKEN_SECONDS:
            problems.append("it claims %d seconds of life, more than an installation token has"
                            % left)
    except Refusal:
        problems.append("it records no expiry")
    if problems:
        raise Refusal("the token file %s is refused: %s" % (path, "; ".join(problems)))
    return token


# GitHub.

class NoRedirect(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):
    """A redirect would carry the bearer elsewhere; every one is refused."""

    def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl):
        raise Refusal("GitHub answered %s %s with a redirect (HTTP %d); redirects are refused"
                      % (req.get_method(), urllib.parse.urlsplit(req.full_url).path, code))


OPENER = urllib.request.build_opener(NoRedirect)


def check_api(api):
    """The API base, refused unless it is exactly https://api.github.com, or plain http to a literal
    loopback address (the selftest's stub)."""
    try:
        u = urllib.parse.urlsplit(api)
        port = u.port
    except ValueError:
        raise Refusal("the API address %s does not parse" % api)
    bare = not (u.username or u.password or u.query or u.fragment or u.path not in ("", "/"))
    if bare and u.scheme == "https" and u.hostname == "api.github.com" and port in (None, 443):
        return api.rstrip("/")
    if bare and u.scheme == "http" and u.hostname:
        try:
            ip = ipaddress.ip_address(u.hostname)
        except ValueError:
            ip = None
        mapped = getattr(ip, "ipv4_mapped", None)
        if ip is not None and mapped is None and ip.is_loopback:
            return api.rstrip("/")
    raise Refusal("the API address %s is neither https://api.github.com nor plain http to a "
                  "loopback address" % api)


class GitHub:
    def __init__(self, api, token):
        self.api = check_api(api)
        self.token = token
        self.remaining = None

    def call(self, method, url, body=None):
        """(status, decoded JSON, headers). Raises RateLimited or Refusal; never prints the body."""
        if not url.startswith(self.api + "/"):
            raise Refusal("refused a request outside %s" % self.api)
        req = urllib.request.Request(url, method=method,
                                     data=json.dumps(body).encode() if body is not None else None)
        req.add_header("Authorization", "Bearer " + self.token)
        req.add_header("Accept", "application/vnd.github+json")
        req.add_header("X-GitHub-Api-Version", "2022-11-28")
        req.add_header("User-Agent", "nifeos-fuzz-filer")
        if body is not None:
            req.add_header("Content-Type", "application/json")
        path = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).path
        try:
            with OPENER.open(req, timeout=30) as resp:
                self.note_rate(resp.headers)
                raw = resp.read()
                return resp.status, (json.loads(raw) if raw else None), resp.headers
        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
            self.note_rate(e.headers)
            try:
                answer = json.loads(e.read())
                msg = str(answer.get("message", ""))
                errors = answer.get("errors") or []
            except (ValueError, AttributeError):
                msg, errors = "", []
            if method != "GET":
                # An answer to a create may echo the advisory back; print only the field names and
                # error codes, which are GitHub's own fixed words.
                words = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z_]{1,40}")
                shown = ["%s:%s" % (x.get("field"), x.get("code")) for x in errors
                         if isinstance(x, dict) and words.fullmatch(str(x.get("field"))) and
                         words.fullmatch(str(x.get("code")))]
                detail = ("the fields and codes " + ", ".join(shown)) if shown else \
                    "its message is not printed, because it may echo the advisory"
            else:
                detail = msg[:200]
            limited = e.code == 429 or (e.code == 403 and (
                self.remaining == 0 or "rate limit" in str(msg).lower() or
                e.headers.get("Retry-After")))
            if limited:
                raise RateLimited("GitHub answered HTTP %d to %s %s (a rate limit; retry after "
                                  "%s seconds)" % (e.code, method, path,
                                                   e.headers.get("Retry-After") or "some"))
            raise Refusal("GitHub answered HTTP %d to %s %s: %s" % (e.code, method, path, detail))
        except urllib.error.URLError as e:
            raise Refusal("could not reach GitHub for %s %s: %s" % (method, path, e.reason))
        except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
            raise Refusal("the answer to %s %s broke off or is not JSON (%s)"
                          % (method, path, type(e).__name__))

    def note_rate(self, headers):
        if headers is None:
            return
        try:
            self.remaining = int(headers.get("X-RateLimit-Remaining"))
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            pass

    def low(self):
        return self.remaining is not None and self.remaining < RATE_FLOOR

    def filed_findings(self):
        """{finding id: advisory id} for every advisory on the repository that carries a Finding
        line, read from every page. Refuses on any failure, so a caller files nothing."""
        found = {}
        url = self.api + ADVISORIES_PATH + "?per_page=100"
        for _ in range(MAX_PAGES):
            status, page, headers = self.call("GET", url)
            if status != 200 or not isinstance(page, list):
                raise Refusal("the advisory listing answered HTTP %d without a list" % status)
            for adv in page:
                if not isinstance(adv, dict):
                    continue
                ghsa = adv.get("ghsa_id")
                for fid in FINDING_LINE.findall(adv.get("description") or ""):
                    if isinstance(ghsa, str) and GHSA_ID.match(ghsa):
                        found.setdefault(fid, ghsa)
            url = next_link(headers.get("Link"), self.api)
            if url is None:
                return found
        raise Refusal("the advisory listing runs past %d pages" % MAX_PAGES)


def next_link(header, api):
    """The `next` URL of a Link header, refused unless it is the same listing on the same API."""
    if not header:
        return None
    for part in header.split(","):
        m = re.match(r'\s*<([^>]*)>\s*;\s*rel="next"\s*$', part)
        if m:
            u = m.group(1)
            if urllib.parse.urlsplit(u).path != ADVISORIES_PATH or \
                    not u.startswith(api + ADVISORIES_PATH + "?"):
                raise Refusal("the advisory listing's next page points elsewhere; refused")
            return u
    return None


# The ledger: an agreement with the programs that read it, held in this code (ledger_state).

def open_ledger(path):
    """(fd of the lock, fd of the ledger, ledger_parse's result). Creates the ledger mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by
    this account, refuses any other shape, and holds an exclusive lock for the run."""
    d = os.path.dirname(path) or "."
    try:
        st = os.lstat(d)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Refusal("the ledger directory %s: %s" % (d, e.strerror))
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) or st.st_uid != os.geteuid() or \
            stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode) != LEDGER_DIR_MODE:
        raise Refusal("the ledger directory %s must be a directory owned by this account, mode "
                      "%04o, and not a link" % (d, LEDGER_DIR_MODE))
    try:
        lock = os.open(path + ".lock", os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC,
                       LEDGER_MODE)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Refusal("the ledger lock %s.lock: %s" % (path, e.strerror))
    try:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        os.close(lock)
        raise Refusal("another run holds the ledger lock")
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_APPEND | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC,
                     LEDGER_MODE)
    except OSError as e:
        os.close(lock)
        raise Refusal("the ledger %s cannot be opened: %s (a link is refused)" % (path, e.strerror))
    try:
        st = os.fstat(fd)
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode) or st.st_uid != os.geteuid() or \
                stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode) != LEDGER_MODE:
            raise Refusal("the ledger %s must be a regular file owned by this account, mode %04o"
                          % (path, LEDGER_MODE))
        chunks = []
        while True:
            b = os.pread(fd, 1 << 16, sum(len(c) for c in chunks))
            if not b:
                break
            chunks.append(b)
        state = ledger_parse(b"".join(chunks).decode(errors="replace"))
    except Refusal:
        os.close(fd)
        os.close(lock)
        raise
    return lock, fd, state


def ledger_parse(text):
    """(state, causes, sigs) from the ledger's text.

    state: {finding id: (state, advisory id or None, utc)}, the last line of each finding winning.
    causes: {signature: (advisory id, later logs, newest commit)}, the last line of each winning.
    sigs: {finding id: signature} for the findings whose line carries one.

    A finding line is `utc<TAB>finding<TAB>pending|filed<TAB>advisory id or -`, with an optional
    fifth field, the signature's short form (a line from before signatures has none). A cause line
    is `utc<TAB>signature<TAB>cause<TAB>advisory id<TAB>count<TAB>commit`. Lines starting with # are
    comments. Any other line refuses the whole ledger."""
    state, causes, sigs = {}, {}, {}
    for n, line in enumerate(text.splitlines(), 1):
        if not line or line.startswith("#"):
            continue
        parts = line.split("\t")
        if len(parts) == 6 and parts[2] == "cause":
            ok = (SIGNATURE_ID.match(parts[1]) and GHSA_ID.match(parts[3]) and
                  parts[4].isdigit() and re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{7,40}", parts[5]))
            if not ok:
                raise Refusal("the ledger's line %d is not a ledger line; nothing is filed until a "
                              "person mends it" % n)
            parse_utc(parts[0])
            causes[parts[1]] = (parts[3], int(parts[4]), parts[5])
            continue
        ok = len(parts) in (4, 5) and FINDING_ID.match(parts[1]) and (
            (parts[2] == "pending" and parts[3] == "-") or
            (parts[2] == "filed" and GHSA_ID.match(parts[3]))) and (
            len(parts) == 4 or SIGNATURE_ID.match(parts[4]))
        if not ok:
            raise Refusal("the ledger's line %d is not a ledger line; nothing is filed until a "
                          "person mends it" % n)
        parse_utc(parts[0])
        state[parts[1]] = (parts[2], None if parts[3] == "-" else parts[3], parts[0])
        if len(parts) == 5:
            sigs[parts[1]] = parts[4]
    return state, causes, sigs


def ledger_state(text):
    """{finding id: (state, advisory id or None, utc)}: the finding lines of ledger_parse."""
    return ledger_parse(text)[0]


def ledger_append(fd, finding, what, ghsa=None, signature=None):
    line = "%s\t%s\t%s\t%s%s\n" % (utc_text(utc_now()), finding, what, ghsa or "-",
                                    ("\t" + signature) if signature else "")
    os.write(fd, line.encode())
    os.fsync(fd)


def cause_append(fd, signature, ghsa, count, commit):
    line = "%s\t%s\tcause\t%s\t%d\t%s\n" % (utc_text(utc_now()), signature, ghsa, count, commit)
    os.write(fd, line.encode())
    os.fsync(fd)


# The findings.

def read_windows(path):
    """{first seed: [(utc, driver, commit, status)]} for each held row of windows.tsv."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Refusal("windows.tsv cannot be opened: %s (a link is refused)" % e.strerror)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(f.fileno()).st_mode):
            raise Refusal("windows.tsv is not a regular file")
        rows = {}
        for raw in f:
            parts = raw.decode(errors="replace").rstrip("\n").split("\t")
            if len(parts) == 8 and parts[6] in HELD_CLASSES and parts[3].isdigit():
                secret(parts[3])
                rows.setdefault(parts[3], []).append((parts[0], parts[1], parts[7], parts[6]))
    return rows


def held_logs(held):
    """[(name, sha256 hex, mtime, replay match or None, slot match or None, cause)] for each regular
    file under the held directory, where cause is (panic source file, message template); see
    cause_of. It reads each log once, under the held directory whose name is the supervisor's, and the count of other entries."""
    try:
        st = os.lstat(held)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Refusal("the held directory cannot be read: %s" % e.strerror)
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) or stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode) & 0o022:
        raise Refusal("the held directory must be a directory, not a link, and writable by its "
                      "owner alone")
    out, other = [], 0
    for name in sorted(os.listdir(held)):
        m = HELD_NAME.match(name)
        if not m:
            other += 1
            continue
        secret(name)
        secret(m.group(1))
        try:
            fd = os.open(os.path.join(held, name), os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC |
                         os.O_NONBLOCK)
        except OSError:
            other += 1
            continue
        with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
            fst = os.fstat(f.fileno())
            if not stat.S_ISREG(fst.st_mode):
                other += 1
                continue
            h = hashlib.sha256()
            replay = slot = None
            panic = after = marked = None
            for raw in f:
                h.update(raw)
                if panic is not None and after is None:
                    after = raw[:MAX_LINE]
                if panic is None and (b"panicked at" in raw or b"PANIC" in raw):
                    panic = raw[:MAX_LINE]
                if marked is None and b"(replay:" in raw:
                    marked = raw[:MAX_LINE]
                if replay is None:
                    replay = REPLAY.search(raw)
                if slot is None:
                    slot = SLOT_LINE.search(raw)
        if replay:
            secret(replay.group(2).decode())
        out.append((name, h.hexdigest(), fst.st_mtime, replay, slot, cause_of(panic, after, marked)))
    return out, other


def template_of(message):
    """The message with its replay suffix removed and each bracketed list, hexadecimal number and
    decimal number replaced by a placeholder, so logs that differ only in seeds, timings and counts
    agree. A number glued to a letter (`u64`) is part of a word and stays."""
    message = REPLAY_SUFFIX.sub("", message)
    message = BRACKETED.sub("[list]", message)
    message = HEX_NUMBER.sub("<hex>", message)
    message = DECIMAL_NUMBER.sub("<n>", message)
    return " ".join(message.split())


def cause_of(panic, after, marked):
    """(source file without line number, message template) from a log's first panic line, the line
    after it, and its first line carrying a replay command (each bytes or None). A panic line that
    does not parse stands whole as the message with the file "-"; a log with no panic line falls
    back to the replay line; a log with neither (a hang) is ("-", "-"). The result is only ever
    hashed into the signature; it is never printed or stored."""
    if panic is not None:
        line = panic.decode(errors="replace").strip()
        m = PANIC_AT.search(line)
        if m:
            message = m.group(1) or m.group(3) or (after or b"").decode(errors="replace")
            return m.group(2), template_of(message)
        return "-", template_of(line)
    if marked is not None:
        return "-", template_of(marked.decode(errors="replace"))
    return "-", "-"


def signature_of(driver, status, cause):
    """The signature's short form: 12 hexadecimal digits of the SHA-256 of its four fields."""
    fields = "\0".join((driver, status, cause[0], cause[1]))
    return hashlib.sha256(fields.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]


def describe(name, digest, replay, slot, windows, cause):
    """The finding's fields for its advisory, or a Refusal naming what does not agree."""
    first = HELD_NAME.match(name).group(1)
    rows = sorted(set(windows.get(first, [])))
    if not rows:
        raise Refusal("windows.tsv holds no held row for it")
    if len({(r[1], r[2], r[3]) for r in rows}) != 1:
        raise Refusal("windows.tsv holds conflicting held rows for it")
    held_at, driver, commit, status = rows[0]
    if driver not in DRIVERS:
        raise Refusal("its row names an unknown driver")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{7,40}", commit):
        raise Refusal("its row's commit is not a commit")
    if slot is not None and (slot.group(1).decode() != driver or slot.group(2).decode() != first):
        raise Refusal("its log and its row name different windows")
    variable = DRIVERS[driver]["variable"]
    if status == "held-finding":
        if replay is None:
            raise Refusal("its row says held-finding and its log holds no replay line")
        if replay.group(1).decode() != variable:
            raise Refusal("its replay line names another driver's variable")
        seed = int(replay.group(2))
        if seed < int(first):
            raise Refusal("its replay seed lies before its window")
        seeds = "%d:1" % seed
    else:
        seeds = "%s:%d" % (first, WINDOW_SEEDS)
    return {"finding": digest[:16], "signature": signature_of(driver, status, cause),
            "class": status, "driver": driver, "commit": commit,
            "held_at": held_at, "seeds": seeds, "variable": variable,
            "filter": DRIVERS[driver]["filter"]}


def advisory_body(f):
    """The create call's body. The summary holds no seed; the description holds the reproducer."""
    if f["class"] == "held-finding":
        seed_line = "- Seed: `%s`" % f["seeds"].split(":")[0]
    else:
        seed_line = "- Seed range (first:count): `%s`" % f["seeds"]
    replay = ("%s=%s NIFE_TEST_FILTER=%s NIFE_TEST_FILTER_ACROSS_IMAGES=1 cargo xtask test"
              % (f["variable"], f["seeds"], f["filter"]))
    description = "\n".join([
        "A finding of nife's continuous fuzz host, filed by fuzz-filer, a program on the host. "
        "It stays private until a person publishes it after the fix, or until 90 days after "
        "this report.",
        "",
        "- Finding: %s" % f["finding"],
        "- Class: %s" % f["class"],
        "- Driver: %s" % f["driver"],
        "- Commit: %s" % f["commit"],
        seed_line,
        "- Held at: %s" % f["held_at"],
        "",
        "Replay, in a checkout of that commit:",
        "",
        "```sh",
        replay,
        "```",
        "",
        "Never copy the seed, the replay line or the guest's output into a pull request, an issue, "
        "a commit message or any other public text before this advisory is published.",
    ])
    return {
        "summary": "Held fuzz finding %s (%s, %s driver)" % (f["finding"], f["class"],
                                                             f["driver"]),
        "description": description,
        "vulnerabilities": [{
            "package": dict(PACKAGE),
            "vulnerable_version_range": "<= %s" % f["commit"],
            "vulnerable_functions": [],
        }],
    }


def check_created(answer, finding):
    """The advisory id GitHub gave, and a list of what is wrong with the draft it made."""
    if not isinstance(answer, dict) or not isinstance(answer.get("ghsa_id"), str) or \
            not GHSA_ID.match(answer["ghsa_id"]):
        raise Refusal("GitHub's answer to the create names no advisory id")
    wrong = []
    if answer.get("state") != "draft":
        wrong.append("its state is %r, not draft" % (answer.get("state"),))
    vulns = answer.get("vulnerabilities")
    ok = isinstance(vulns, list) and vulns and all(
        isinstance(v, dict) and isinstance(v.get("package"), dict) and
        v["package"].get("ecosystem") and v["package"].get("name") and
        v.get("vulnerable_version_range") for v in vulns)
    if not ok:
        wrong.append("it lacks a package or a vulnerable version range, so it cannot be published")
    if finding not in FINDING_LINE.findall(answer.get("description") or ""):
        wrong.append("its description lost the Finding line")
    return answer["ghsa_id"], wrong


# The run.

def run(args):
    token = read_token(args.token_file, args.token_group)
    github = GitHub(args.api, token)
    home = args.fuzz_home
    lock, fd, ledger = open_ledger(args.ledger)
    try:
        return file_findings(args, github, home, fd, ledger)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
        os.close(lock)


def file_findings(args, github, home, fd, parsed):
    ledger, causes, sigs = parsed
    held = os.path.join(home, "state", "held")
    logs, other = held_logs(held)
    windows = read_windows(os.path.join(home, "state", "windows.tsv")) if logs else {}
    if other:
        say("the held directory holds %d entries that are not held logs; they are not read"
            % other, err=True)
    now = time.time()
    refused = 0
    # One group per signature, its logs oldest first; each entry is (fields, age, mtime).
    groups, seen = {}, set()
    for name, digest, mtime, replay, slot, cause in sorted(logs, key=lambda e: (e[2], e[0])):
        fid = digest[:16]
        age = age_text(now - mtime)
        if fid in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(fid)
        filed_before = ledger.get(fid, ("",))[0] == "filed"
        try:
            f = describe(name, digest, replay, slot, windows, cause)
        except Refusal as e:
            if not filed_before:
                refused += 1
                say("finding %s (held %s) is refused: %s" % (fid, age, e), err=True)
            continue
        groups.setdefault(f["signature"], []).append((f, age, mtime))

    # Signatures an advisory already covers, by advisory id: the cause lines, and the filed
    # findings (a line from before signatures has none; its own log's signature stands for it).
    covered = {sig: v[0] for sig, v in causes.items()}
    for fid, sig in sigs.items():
        if ledger.get(fid, ("",))[0] == "filed":
            covered.setdefault(sig, ledger[fid][1])
    for sig, entries in groups.items():
        for f, _, _ in entries:
            if ledger.get(f["finding"], ("",))[0] == "filed":
                covered.setdefault(sig, ledger[f["finding"]][1])

    def note(sig, ghsa):
        """Record, once it changes, how many later logs share the signature and the newest commit."""
        entries = groups[sig]
        newest = max(entries, key=lambda e: e[2])[0]["commit"]
        want = (ghsa, len(entries) - 1, newest)
        if causes.get(sig) != want:
            cause_append(fd, sig, *want)
            causes[sig] = want

    todo = []
    for sig, entries in groups.items():
        if sig in covered:
            if not args.dry_run:
                note(sig, covered[sig])
            continue
        pending = [e for e in entries if ledger.get(e[0]["finding"], ("",))[0] == "pending"]
        todo.append((sig, (pending or entries)[0]))
    filed = len(covered)
    for sig, entries in groups.items():
        if len(entries) > 1:
            say("cause %s: %d held logs, one advisory" % (sig, len(entries)))
    if not todo:
        say("%d held logs, %d causes, %d filed before, none to file" % (len(seen), len(groups),
                                                                       filed))
        return 1 if refused else 0
    if args.dry_run:
        for sig, (f, age, _) in todo:
            say("would file finding %s (held %s) for cause %s (%d held logs)"
                % (f["finding"], age, sig, len(groups[sig])))
        return 1 if refused else 0

    try:
        on_github = github.filed_findings()
    except RateLimited as e:
        say("%s; nothing is filed this run" % e, err=True)
        return EX_TEMPFAIL
    except Refusal as e:
        say("%s; nothing is filed this run, so nothing is filed twice" % e, err=True)
        return 1

    def on_github_ghsa(sig):
        for f, _, _ in groups[sig]:
            if f["finding"] in on_github:
                return on_github[f["finding"]]
        return None

    created = 0
    for i, (sig, (f, age, _)) in enumerate(todo):
        fid = f["finding"]
        ghsa = on_github_ghsa(sig)
        if ghsa is not None:
            for g, gage, _ in groups[sig]:
                if g["finding"] in on_github and ledger.get(g["finding"], ("",))[0] != "filed":
                    ledger_append(fd, g["finding"], "filed", on_github[g["finding"]], sig)
                    say("finding %s (held %s) is already advisory %s; recorded"
                        % (g["finding"], gage, on_github[g["finding"]]))
            note(sig, ghsa)
            continue
        if created >= args.max:
            left = sum(1 for s2, _ in todo[i:] if on_github_ghsa(s2) is None)
            say("%d findings wait for the next run (at most %d a run)" % (left, args.max))
            break
        if github.low():
            say("GitHub reports %d requests left this hour; the rest wait for the next run"
                % github.remaining, err=True)
            return EX_TEMPFAIL
        if created:
            time.sleep(args.pace)
        ledger_append(fd, fid, "pending", None, sig)
        try:
            status, answer, _ = github.call("POST", github.api + ADVISORIES_PATH, advisory_body(f))
        except RateLimited as e:
            say("finding %s (held %s): %s; the rest wait for the next run" % (fid, age, e),
                err=True)
            return EX_TEMPFAIL
        except Refusal as e:
            refused += 1
            say("finding %s (held %s) was not filed: %s; the next run looks for it on GitHub "
                "before it files again" % (fid, age, e), err=True)
            continue
        created += 1
        if status != 201:
            refused += 1
            say("finding %s (held %s): the create answered HTTP %d, not 201" % (fid, age, status),
                err=True)
            continue
        try:
            ghsa, wrong = check_created(answer, fid)
        except Refusal as e:
            refused += 1
            say("finding %s (held %s): %s; the next run looks for it on GitHub" % (fid, age, e),
                err=True)
            continue
        ledger_append(fd, fid, "filed", ghsa, sig)
        note(sig, ghsa)
        say("filed finding %s (held %s) as %s for cause %s (%d held logs)"
            % (fid, age, ghsa, sig, len(groups[sig])))
        for w in wrong:
            refused += 1
            say("advisory %s for finding %s: %s" % (ghsa, fid, w), err=True)
    return 1 if refused else 0


def show_ledger(args):
    try:
        with open(args.ledger, "rb") as f:
            state, causes, _ = ledger_parse(f.read().decode(errors="replace"))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        state, causes = {}, {}
    now = utc_now()
    for fid, (what, ghsa, when) in sorted(state.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1][2]):
        print("%s\t%s\t%s\t%s ago" % (fid, what, ghsa or "-",
                                      age_text((now - parse_utc(when)).total_seconds())))
    for sig, (ghsa, count, commit) in sorted(causes.items()):
        print("cause %s\t%s\t%d later logs\tnewest commit %s" % (sig, ghsa, count, commit))
    return 0


def main(argv):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="fuzz-filer",
                                 description="File each held fuzz finding as a private advisory.")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="command", required=True)
    r = sub.add_parser("run", help="file every held finding that has no advisory yet")
    r.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="send nothing; print what would be filed")
    r.add_argument("--max", type=int, default=DEFAULT_MAX, help="advisories to create a run")
    r.add_argument("--fuzz-home", default=None,
                   help="the supervisor's NIFE_FUZZ_HOME (default: that variable, else ~/fuzz)")
    r.add_argument("--ledger", default=DEFAULT_LEDGER)
    r.add_argument("--token-file", default=DEFAULT_TOKEN_FILE)
    r.add_argument("--token-group", default=DEFAULT_TOKEN_GROUP)
    r.add_argument("--api", default=DEFAULT_API)
    r.add_argument("--pace", type=float, default=DEFAULT_PACE, help="seconds between creates")
    r.set_defaults(run=run)
    g = sub.add_parser("ledger", help="print the ledger: ids, states, advisory ids, ages")
    g.add_argument("--ledger", default=DEFAULT_LEDGER)
    g.set_defaults(run=show_ledger)
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if args.command == "run":
        if args.fuzz_home is None:
            args.fuzz_home = os.environ.get("NIFE_FUZZ_HOME") or \
                os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), "fuzz")
        if args.max < 1:
            ap.error("--max must be at least 1")
    try:
        return args.run(args)
    except Refusal as e:
        say(e, err=True)
        return 3
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001; a traceback could carry a seed in a local's repr
        say("internal error (%s); nothing more is printed, because the message could carry a "
            "seed or the token" % type(e).__name__, err=True)
        return 4


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
